      "proposed_content": "The source's exceptional cases form an adversarial hierarchy for numerical verification: interval displacements and clusters defeat one-root-per-Gram-interval assumptions, low-amplitude close pairs are harder than ordinary occupancy failures, and the most ambiguous pairs force fine-mesh or smaller-remainder recomputation.",
