      "proposed_content": "The paper contrasts two finite search strategies: extending a contiguous verified prefix yields a stronger but still bounded-height statement, whereas increasingly frequent Gram-law failures and a term-level near-cancellation mechanism motivate targeted searches in selected remote neighborhoods where especially delicate behavior is expected.",
